<figure>
	<figuretitle>Hey, Hey, We're The Monkeys</figuretitle>
	<p>There are four species of monkey are native to the forests of Costa
Rica:, the Central American squirrel monkey (Saimiri oerstedii), the
Panamanian white-faced capuchin (Cebus imitator), the mantled howler
(Alouatta palliata) and Geoffroy's spider monkey (Ateles geoffroyi).
This little guy is a white-faced capuchin.</p>
	<img src="20220520_123944.jpg" />
</figure>

